  "beats": {
    "B1": {
      "file": "audio/beats/B1.wav",
      "duration": 8.11,
      "sha256": "5886f05b108a936a496a91dd0b77dd7d0e89656e140563cba7cbbe373c0733ce",
      "sentence_pause_seconds": 0.35,
      "sentences": [
        {
          "index": 0,
          "text": "In Babergh and Mid Suffolk, in eastern England, historic roofs do not all look alike.",
          "start": 0.0,
          "end": 4.88,
          "cache_key": "5ade9867934a84370281a9b6e203ffebfe9e3d7729eafa738918d6976553e4ca"
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "text": "Some rise steeply. Others sit noticeably lower.",
          "start": 5.23,
          "end": 8.11,
          "cache_key": "229881b909c8e4924da37a6ef121c6214c1102c2927af8c66ff9ebe2af34da84"
        }
      ]
    },
    "B2": {
      "file": "audio/beats/B2.wav",
      "duration": 13.62,
      "sha256": "a642c27c906d629a693812c427096c51e34a874c8ab3849af1fec8d30fc1322e",
      "sentence_pause_seconds": 0.35,
      "sentences": [
        {
          "index": 0,
          "text": "Older timber-framed buildings here were probably roofed with thatch or oak shingles, depending on which materials were available.",
          "start": 0.0,
          "end": 6.93,
          "cache_key": "c4a60857ba1399c7ec76e5d13afa6a57232bb3c94ffd50637debe9c2a6612e6e"
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "text": "Longstraw thatch, the most traditional covering in these districts, is laid at a steep pitch of about fifty degrees.",
          "start": 7.28,
          "end": 13.62,
          "cache_key": "35ec1ca19c1b3d16808c4298a64a50362c394f5c95f3573f417d224b90fb6887"
        }
      ]
    },
    "B3": {
      "file": "audio/beats/B3.wav",
      "duration": 8.97,
      "sha256": "d8bd6f23e6a85e3c9a80da2ee198f1e20a8c442005fb1e8227acb0c95354c5c4",
      "sentence_pause_seconds": 0.35,
      "sentences": [
        {
          "index": 0,
          "text": "Eventually, clay peg tiles replaced some of these thatched roofs.",
          "start": 0.0,
          "end": 3.86,
          "cache_key": "40687d056c6b1bd5ffdf151d2d2269f6407b5d22d16e06bafc794ae2ff1940c7"
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "text": "Plain clay tile roofs are fairly steep too, typically forty-five degrees or more.",
          "start": 4.21,
          "end": 8.97,
          "cache_key": "4c1c1547cad913fcfa370bc6914b06eba1b32e46d82b86b03b51454c3d1d54e5"
        }
      ]
    },
    "B4": {
      "file": "audio/beats/B4.wav",
      "duration": 15.84,
      "sha256": "27855e8e64990d6516c3aee7a26d53b1e144649b9533cd8e017668c7db0bce04",
      "sentence_pause_seconds": 0.35,
      "sentences": [
        {
          "index": 0,
          "text": "Materials also began to travel further.",
          "start": 0.0,
          "end": 2.35,
          "cache_key": "a13e1f4d9da48f44fb26fcc72b89298a4dbd06d24d99881a723a5d82a3419213"
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "text": "From the eighteenth century, clay pantiles were used more commonly, as moving materials around the country became easier.",
          "start": 2.7,
          "end": 9.57,
          "cache_key": "3c5e240e43605c9fb5a37d1bfcccb276112c489668a54474294bd46ced0c4e1a"
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "text": "In the nineteenth century, the railways meant that slate from Wales, Cornwall and Cumbria was often used here.",
          "start": 9.92,
          "end": 15.84,
          "cache_key": "81188502c076fffb7d2a7a4dfa920054ff5b7b8191a3afd99b60ec222ba98c06"
        }
      ]
    },
    "B5": {
      "file": "audio/beats/B5.wav",
      "duration": 9.37,
      "sha256": "bec2278619a3f763428e08253da6f863ab004d23c3722ded4bcc1611e4ec56bc",
      "sentence_pause_seconds": 0.35,
      "sentences": [
        {
          "index": 0,
          "text": "Slate behaves differently.",
          "start": 0.0,
          "end": 1.7,
          "cache_key": "0279e30a85d3c5acc868c670afbae509cf7c5aaeffafbffde8f50619a9a29eca"
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "text": "Slate roofs here are usually pitched at around thirty degrees, and slate is more effective than smaller tiles at a lower pitch.",
          "start": 2.05,
          "end": 9.37,
          "cache_key": "41eff17af1f131754f07022a1428aeba52e2358da009c81afd3e5ea0a1b717b7"
        }
      ]
    },
    "B6": {
      "file": "audio/beats/B6.wav",
      "duration": 11.85,
      "sha256": "c3509466578748af501bb18f4ca0a2c1bb28148baab4954678a8ec839e04d49a",
      "sentence_pause_seconds": 0.35,
      "sentences": [
        {
          "index": 0,
          "text": "Thatch, clay tile and slate each have a typical pitch.",
          "start": 0.0,
          "end": 3.16,
          "cache_key": "9599198fc91959c6a7653ee9b6bbee57d3d92a7a3b7ec2c170a5c38e5448015d"
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "text": "These are tendencies, not rules, and not every building followed the same path.",
          "start": 3.51,
          "end": 8.04,
          "cache_key": "0f93841c86f34b69159a0739a4349e29e3144bbd3abb210b9dc8ee3e34e3d98a"
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "text": "But the pitch of an old roof can still be a clue to its covering.",
          "start": 8.39,
          "end": 11.85,
          "cache_key": "733c1ca8ee91c37e19b755300f9936566eca6506ef464fa01c57f39159847076"
        }
      ]
    }
  },
